[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:80. The Crystal Palace]
[00:00.640]Passage 80 | 文章八十
[00:02.075]The Crystal Palace. | 水晶宫。
[00:04.780]Perhaps the most extraordinary building of the 19th century | 也许19世纪最不寻常的建筑
[00:10.120]was the Crystal Palace, | 是水晶宫，
[00:12.205]which was built in Hyde Park for the Great Exhibition of 1851. | 它是为1851年的万国博览会在海德公园建造的。
[00:17.945]The Crystal Palace was different from all other buildings in the world, | 水晶宫与世界上所有其他建筑都不同，
[00:23.540]for it was made of iron and glass. | 因为它是由钢铁和玻璃建造的。
[00:27.475]It was one of the biggest buildings of all time, | 它是有史以来最大的建筑之一，
[00:31.760]and a lot of people from many countries came to see it. | 许多来自世界各地的人们都前来参观。
[00:36.040]A great many goods were sent to the exhibition from various parts of the world. | 许多商品从世界各地被送到展览会上。
[00:42.280]There was also a great deal of machinery on display. | 还有大量的机器展出。
[00:46.910]The most wonderful piece of machinery on show | 展出的最奇妙的机器
[00:51.085]was Naysmith's steam hammer. | 是纳史密斯蒸汽锤。
[00:53.900]Though in those days traveling was not as easy as it is today, | 尽管在那些日子里旅行不像今天这样容易，
[00:58.510]steamboats carried thousands of visitors across the Channel from Europe. | 但汽船载着成千上万的游客从欧洲横渡英吉利海峡。
[01:04.045]On arriving in England, | 抵达英国后，
[01:06.440]they were taken to the Crystal Palace by train. | 他们乘火车前往水晶宫。
[01:10.300]There were six million visitors in all, | 总共有六百万游客，
[01:14.315]and the profits from the exhibition were used to build museums and colleges. | 展览的利润被用来建造博物馆和大学。
[01:19.965]Later, | 后来，
[01:21.545]the Crystal Palace was moved to South London. | 水晶宫被搬到了南伦敦。
[01:25.155]It remained one of the most famous buildings in the world | 它一直是世界上最著名的建筑之一，
[01:29.145]until it was burned down in 1936. | 直到1936年被烧毁。